# F.9.18 section reductions for the moving linear-two orbit

The literal source representation admits the valid maximal-section dichotomy
once the bounded faithful elementary actor and the two no-strong-FF assertions
are supplied. Its noncentral branch gives FF-modules on both faithful section
images. Its centralized branch constructs an actual Irr⁺ section whose ambient
orbit spans Ũ_H. The canonical factor-space lemmas transfer the centralizer
identity from F.9.18(5iii) into cross-factor fixation in both directions.

The full B.4.2 exclusion, the T-homogeneous choice, and the refinement of the
complete F.9.18(5) list into the natural/orthogonal alternatives remain open.
In particular these conditional results do not yet establish the three module
alternatives of 13.8.16(1). Final assembly remains in this module's task.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.8.16(1), printed p.952 (PDF p.969), and F.9.18, pp.325–326.
-/
